      "content": "Given that 8 liters is 20% of the capacity of one container, we need to find the total capacity of 40 such containers.\n\nFirst, let's determine the full capacity of one container. If 8 liters is 20% of the container's capacity, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 0.20 \\times \\text{capacity} = 8 \\text{ liters} \\]\n\nTo find the full capacity, we divide both sides by 0.20:\n\\[ \\text{capacity} = \\frac{8 \\text{ liters}}{0.20} = 40 \\text{ liters} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the total capacity of 40 such containers. Since each container has a capacity of 40 liters, the total capacity for 40 containers is:\n\\[ 40 \\times 40 \\text{ liters} = 1600 \\text{ liters} \\]\n\nLet's verify the result:\n- We know 8 liters is 20% of one container, so 40 liters is 100% of one container.\n- For 40 containers, the total capacity is 40 times 40 liters, which is 1600 liters.\n\nThus, the total capacity of 40 containers is 1600 liters.\n\nFINAL: 1600",
